  "executive_briefing": "As of mid-2026, the global corporate tax landscape remains dominated by the structural divide between the U.S. domestic minimum tax framework and the OECD Pillar Two regime. While the international consensus on a 15% minimum tax persists, fiscal sovereignty is asserting itself through domestic policy adjustments and targeted rebates in regions like ASEAN. Concurrently, the transition to mandatory, real-time structured e-invoicing has moved from exploratory pilots to rigid, multi-year enforcement cycles, particularly in Singapore. International trade remains in a period of high volatility as legal challenges to U.S. executive tariff authority create significant uncertainty for multinational supply chains, moving the regulatory focus from tariff adoption to judicial reconciliation.",
